# Text files are stored, and checked out on every OS, with LF line endings.
# Without this a Windows checkout follows core.autocrlf and gets CRLF, and
# the tests that read a repository file (the docs table the stream-chunk test
# parses, the workflow guards) failed on main's Windows legs only: twice, for
# eleven pushes the second time (#486, #504). tests/ci_workflows/ checks this
# line is here.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Byte-exact fuzz inputs: the SSE parser's seeds carry CRLF and lone CR on
# purpose, so no seed is ever converted.
fuzz/seeds/** -text
